cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "datasource-flowref-decompiler: a faithful-or-refuse decompiler over flowref"
abstract: >
  Point it at a binary and get back compilable C. A control-flow-aware decompiler in
  Lean 4, built on the flowref xref finder, under a faithful-or-refuse contract: it
  emits C it can justify against the machine code or it declines, rather than
  emitting something plausible and leaving the reader to find out which. That
  contract is the reason the whole thing is in a proof language.
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    email: ernest.lee@chibifire.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4570-1436"
version: 0.1.0-dev.1
date-released: "2026-08-17"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/fire/datasource-flowref-decompiler"
keywords:
  - lean4
  - decompiler
  - reverse-engineering
  - formal-methods
